Example 19: SQS via random sampling for equimolar fcc CoCrFeNi
================================================================

Physical system
---------------
CoCrFeNi is the common equiatomic face-centred-cubic Cantor-alloy subsystem.
This example uses a 2x2x2 conventional fcc supercell with 32 metal sites:
8 Co, 8 Cr, 8 Fe, and 8 Ni. The number of labelled arrangements is
32!/(8!^4) ~ 10^17, so full enumeration is not practical. Instead, SOD first
draws many uniform random configurations and then selects the best Special
Quasirandom Structure (SQS) from that sampled ensemble.

Workflow
--------
1. sod_random.sh -nconf 20000 -sym on -seed 20260710
   randomsod draws 20,000 uniform configurations at the equimolar CoCrFeNi
   composition, folds them to full Fm-3m symmetry representatives using the
   committed EQMATRIX, and writes n08_08_08/random/ENSEMBLE.

2. sod_sqs.sh (run from n08_08_08/random/)
   sqssod scores each sampled configuration against ideal random quaternary
   mixing using species-resolved pair probabilities. INSQS sets MaxOrder=2
   and a 6.0 Angstrom pair cutoff, covering four fcc pair orbits in this
   supercell. Rankings are written to n08_08_08/random/OUTSQS and the detailed
   pair-channel table for the best configuration is written to SQS_CORRELATIONS.

3. sod_gener.sh -choose 9367 (run from n08_08_08/random/)
   Writes the selected SQS as n08_08_08/random/c09367/configuration.cif
   (FILER=0).

Files
-----
  INSOD                                      SOD input (32 fcc metal sites, 8/8/8/8 composition)
  SGO                                        Fm-3m space-group operators (space group 225)
  OPERATORS                                  Supercell operator list
  EQMATRIX                                   Equivalence matrix required for -sym on
  supercell.cif                              Parent fcc supercell geometry
  n08_08_08/random/INSQS                     Pair SQS parameters (MaxOrder=2, cutoff 6.0 A)
  n08_08_08/random/OUTSQS                    Top-10 SQS ranking for the sampled ensemble
  n08_08_08/random/SQS_CORRELATIONS          Best-configuration pair-channel probabilities
  n08_08_08/random/c09367/configuration.cif  Selected SQS structure

The sampled ensemble itself is not shipped, because it is about 1.4 MB. Run
step 1 below to regenerate it:

  n08_08_08/random/ENSEMBLE                  20,000 symmetry-folded random configurations (step 1)

How to run
----------
From the example19 directory:

    sod_random.sh -nconf 20000 -sym on -seed 20260710

Then rank the random sample and write the selected structure:

    cd n08_08_08/random
    sod_sqs.sh
    sod_gener.sh -choose 9367

The final equimolar INSOD is intentionally too large for full enumeration.
If you change the cell or composition, regenerate the symmetry files using a
temporary zero-substitution INSOD before running the random-sampling workflow;
do not use full enumeration for the 8/8/8/8 composition.

Expected output
---------------
20,000 configurations in n08_08_08/random/ENSEMBLE.
OUTSQS rank 1: configuration c09367, Error = 5.0455729E-03.
The matched random-alloy diameter L is 0.0 Angstrom for the best sampled
configuration because none of the four pair shells is matched exactly within
the requested tolerance.
